    "# Brain Tumor MRI Classification: Group 4\n",
    "\n",
    "**TLDR of code production:**\n",
    "1. Loads in brain MRI pictures (Includes all 4 types: glioma, meningioma, pituitary, and no tumor)\n",
    "2. Trains one small CNN several times, changing one feature at a time to conduct an ablation study:\n",
    "   * **Augmentation study:** randomly tweaks training pictures so the model sees more variety (Models 1 to 4).\n",
    "   * **Normalization study:** rescaling pixel values in different ways before the model sees them\n",
    "3. Repeats each experiment with 3 random seeds (6 total experiments x 3 seeds =  18 runs) and compares the scores\n",
    "\n",
    "Below is a table outlining the experiements conducted along with the normalization and augmentation techniques implemented:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Experiment | Normalization | Augmentation |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| `baseline_no_normalization` | none | none |\n",
    "| `model1_baseline` | dataset | none |\n",
    "| `baseline_image_normalization` | image | none |\n",
    "| `model2_geometric_intensity` | dataset | Small shifts and rotations, brightness and contrast changes |\n",
    "| `model3_noise_blur_compression` | dataset | Gaussian noise, Gaussian blur, JPEG compression |\n",
    "| `model4_combined` | dataset | Everything from Models 2 and 3 |\n",
    "\n",
    "`model1_baseline` is shared by both studies. Normalization is compared on the baseline (no augmentation), and augmentation is compared with dataset normalization."
   ]
